\title{Polynomial Commitment Schemes}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    The component that turns an oracle in an [IOP](dhsorens-002E) into something a real verifier can query. Swapping the commitment scheme changes a system's proof size, its trust assumptions, and its post-quantum status while leaving the [arithmetisation](dhsorens-002R) untouched — which is why this is the layer where systems are usually differentiated.
}

\p{
    [ArkLib](dhsorens-0040) splits these into ordinary and functional commitments; understanding why that split is the right one is part of the point of these pages.
}

